---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Journal — Devina Azaria" description="Curated learning notes and selected historical writing from Devina Azaria's portfolio archive.">
<section class="shell section page-intro">
  <div class="eyebrow">Journal</div>
  <h1>Learning in public, over time.</h1>
  <p class="lead">This journal preserves selected historical writing and learning notes from the earlier version of devina.id. Older material is being reviewed carefully so that only relevant, attributable work is carried into the new portfolio.</p>
</section>

<section class="shell section">
  <div class="grid journal-grid">
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <div class="tag">Learning Journey</div>
      <h2>Coding Journey</h2>
      <p class="muted">A curated timeline of coding and technology learning discovered in the legacy archive, beginning with early coding-interest articles and later learning-roadmap material.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/journal/coding-journey/">Open Coding Journey →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <div class="tag">Technology</div>
      <h3>AI & Digital Literacy</h3>
      <p class="muted">Selected explainers and reflections on artificial intelligence, digital services, and technology will be migrated only after authorship and context are verified.</p>
      <span class="status">Migration review in progress</span>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <div class="tag">Culture & Creative</div>
      <h3>Culture, Music & Communication</h3>
      <p class="muted">Historical material related to culture, creative tools, music, and communication will be separated from generic editorial content and preserved where it supports the portfolio story.</p>
      <span class="status">Migration review in progress</span>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell section archive-note">
  <div class="eyebrow">Migration Note</div>
  <h2>Curated, not copied wholesale.</h2>
  <p class="lead">The previous WordPress site mixed personal learning content with SEO, commerce, recipes, catalog material, and other experiments. The new journal keeps useful history without presenting every legacy post as a personal achievement or original work.</p>
</section>
</BaseLayout>